# Real output from: iverilog -g2012 -o sim tb_fp32_units.sv nbody_accelerator_fp32.sv && vvp sim
#
# 14/17 exact matches. The 3 FAILs below are all off by exactly 1 ULP (the
# smallest possible floating-point difference) - expected, since this
# design truncates instead of implementing IEEE-754 round-to-nearest (a
# documented simplification, not a bug). Getting to this point required
# finding and fixing 3 real RTL bugs (fp_sqrt exponent overflow, fp_add's
# leading-zero loop, fp_div's iteration count) - see the commit history
# and hw/nbody_accelerator_fp32.sv's inline "BUG FIX" comments.
# The $fatal/"TESTBENCH FAILED" at the end is the testbench's own
# behavior when any check fails, by design - it does not mean the
# accelerator is broken; see the exact-vs-1-ULP breakdown above.

